# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
# This file must sit at the root of the published output (public/), named
# `_redirects` with no extension. It is the live copy; seo/redirects/ keeps the
# Apache equivalent for reference if the host ever changes.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves clean URLs: diensten.html is served at /diensten, and
# /diensten.html 301s to /diensten automatically. Targets below are therefore
# written extensionless, matching the canonical tags.
#
# Dutch lives in /nl/ alongside /en/, so the bare root MUST be sent somewhere —
# without the rule below, vonkelektra.nl serves nothing. It is the one redirect
# every visitor and every crawl of the homepage passes through, so it has to be
# a single 301 straight to the destination: never / -> /nl -> /nl/, and never
# language-sniffed (Googlebot crawls from the US with no Accept-Language header,
# so a negotiated redirect would hide one locale from it entirely).
#
# Cloudflare Pages limits: 2,000 static rules, 100 with a splat (*). We use 3.
# Query strings (e.g. /?p=123) are NOT matchable here — use a Redirect Rule in
# the Cloudflare dashboard for those.

# =====================================================================
# THE RULES THAT ACTUALLY MATTER — the live WordPress site being replaced
# =====================================================================
# vonkelektra.nl is a live WordPress site today with six indexed pages. Those
# URLs carry the ranking and inbound links the business already has, and every
# one of them 404s the moment this site replaces it unless it is mapped here.
# Everything below this block is prototype housekeeping with no traffic behind it.
#
# VERIFY THE RIGHT-HAND COLUMN BEFORE DEPLOYING. Three old pages collapse onto
# one new /diensten, and which anchor each lands on is a judgement call about
# your own content.
#
# This list came from the live navigation and is not necessarily complete. Pull
# the full set from Google Search Console (Pages report) or crawl the live site,
# and add anything missing before switching DNS.

/                       /nl/                         301

/over/                  /nl/over-ons                 301
/contact/               /nl/contact                  301
/duurzameoplossingen/   /nl/diensten#zonnepanelen    301
/elektrawerkzaamheden/  /nl/diensten#meterkast       301
/klussenenonderhoud/    /nl/diensten#onderhoud       301

# /cookiebeleid — the old cookie policy. The new site sets no cookies, so there
# is nothing to point this at yet. Send it to the privacy page once that exists.
# /cookiebeleid         /nl/privacybeleid            301

# Old WordPress plumbing Google has crawled and will keep requesting.
/wp-content/*           /nl/                         301
/wp-admin/*             /nl/                         301
/feed/                  /nl/                         301
# For /?p=123 style permalinks, add a Redirect Rule in the dashboard instead —
# _redirects cannot match a query string.

